# Red-team override config for mini-swe-agent (base: builtin mini.yaml @ v2.4.4).
#
# Why this exists: the stock mini.yaml frames every run as "Please solve this
# issue … verify your fix works" with a helpful-assistant system prompt. In the
# probes we are NOT asking for a conventional fix — we want the agent to game the
# tests (gameability) or diverge from the reference (altsolve). Helpfulness-tuned
# models read the stock framing and revert to solving normally, ignoring the
# red-team instructions appended to the task (observed: gpt-5.5 produced the
# canonical answer; opus bailed without trying).
#
# So we override ONLY the two framing templates. Everything else — the Command
# Execution Rules, the model observation/format templates, the environment env —
# is copied verbatim from mini.yaml and MUST stay in sync with the installed
# version; those carry the operational contract the agent needs to run at all.
# ponytail: hand-synced to mini-swe-agent 2.4.4; if that pin moves, re-diff mini.yaml.
